WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:01.870
For more information visit www.fema.org

00:03:00.188 --> 00:03:01.388
Oh, that's it.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.290
I want to see you, Mr. Hanna.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.530
What's the matter?

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:37.390
Somebody pay that bill?

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.890
We want money.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.250
Yes, money.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:41.460
You want your money?

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.500
We want to get paid.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.590
Oh, you want my money.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.450
Is that fair? Do I want your money?

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.180
Suppose George Washington's soldiers had asked for money.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.280
Where would this country be today?

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.440
But they did ask.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.330
And where's Washington?

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.270
No, my friends, no.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.160
Money will never make you happy.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.760
And happy will never make you money.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.840
That might be a wisecrack, but I doubt it.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.060
We want our money.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:03.730
I'll make you all a promise.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.730
If you'd all stick with me and work hard, we'd forget about money.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.680
Let's get together and we'd make a regular hotel out of this place.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.980
I'll put writing paper in the hotel.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.040
And next year, if you behave yourself, I'll put an envelope.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.630
I'm going to put extra blankets free in all your rooms.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:18.570
There'll be no cup of charge.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.890
Think, think of the opportunities here in Florida.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.690
Three years ago, I came to Florida without a nickel in my pocket.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.150
Now I've got a nickel in my pocket.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.910
That's all very well, Mr. Hammer.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:29.980
We have been paying...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:37.020
two weeks and we want our wages wages you want to be wage slaves answer me that no no of course

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:44.160
not but what makes wage slaves wages i want you to be free remember there's nothing like liberty

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:49.970
except colliers in the sad evening post be free my friends one for all and all for me and me for

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:55.470
you and three for five and six for a quarter pardon me a couple of telegrams for you mr hammer

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:59.970
there you are business is beginning to pick up already a few boys will own

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.620
Let me be calm.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:04.640
We arrived this afternoon on the 4.30.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.820
Kindly reserve two floors and three ceilings.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:08.810
Must be mice.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.160
If we liked your property, we would immediately buy it.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.870
See that? Things have started our way already.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:15.710
Who is it from?

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:17.580
Western Union.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.250
And they've got a lot of money, too.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:21.950
On the 4.15, eh?

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.780
Well, I'll take the bus down myself.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.220
Here's another one, Mr. Hammer.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.020
See?

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.660
We're gonna be stuffed by tonight.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.980
This hotel will be so crowded that we'll be turning away...

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.410
If there's another hotel in Coconut Beach, cancel our reservations.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.330
I knew it. It was too good.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:39.740
Wait a minute. P.S.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.020
Ann Fanny had an eight-pound boy. Can you come to the wedding?

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:47.180
You see, everything is all right, boys. Everything is all right.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:50.060
You're all invited to the wedding of Ann Fanny's eight-pound boy.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.240
However, that won't be for a couple of years yet.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:57.250
In the meantime, I want you to buck up. Get down to work.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.980
Let's put this thing over with a bang, and...

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.480
Above all, forget about money. Don't think of it.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.480
Just forget about it because you won't get it anyway.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:07.780
Thank you.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.660
See that? I keep them dancing for their money.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.960
Jamison, I'm going down. I'll meet the 415.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.480
If I never come back, you'll know I'm still waiting for the train.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:46.880
Yes, sir.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:50.100
And in my absence, I'm relying on you to take good care of everything.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.420
You can depend upon me, sir.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:53.600
That's fine. If any guests come in, take good care of them.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:53.840
Yeah.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.070
And think of me, Jamison.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:55.870
You bet I will.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:56.830
I'll be back someday.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.940
Keep a light burning in the window.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:07:59.380
Yes, sir.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.240
All right, sir. Goodbye, James. Goodbye.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:11.260
Hello, Harvey. Why so downhearted?

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.970
Is Bob Adams cutting you out with Polly Potter?

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.450
I'm not worried about a hotel clerk.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.910
No, but I'll bet you're worried about a Potter million.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.150
You generally could use money in the old days.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:23.550
I'll lay off that stuff.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.740
You know, marrying Polly is the only way for you to square your debt.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:28.410
I can take care of myself.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.260
I doubt it.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.860
Suppose I have a little plan that'll take care of both of us.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:35.740
What do you mean?

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.220
Have you ever seen that diamond necklace of Mrs. Potter's?

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:40.300
You bet I have.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.080
What's that got to do with us?

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:47.780
The room and my room are right next to each other.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.600
Hers is 318, mine 320.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.130
The door between is unlocked.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:53.940
Well?

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:57.490
She keeps everything in a jewel case locked up in her dresser.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.520
The key is always in her bag.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.960
It's a large order, but maybe it can be done.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.240
Suppose I invite Mrs. Potter and Polly

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.860
to take supper with me tonight.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:09.870
What then?

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.130
Sometime during the evening

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.890
I might be able to get the key out of her bag.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:16.910
Now you're talking.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.280
That sounds more like old time.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.710
And I'll try to get rid of Bob Adams for you.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.050
What do you know of that hill?

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.000
What a question.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.580
Do I know that cunning little hill?

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.140
It's cunning, all right.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.500
But that's why there hasn't been any development here.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:39.720
Couldn't it be cut out?

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:41.270
Too expensive.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:42.660
Now, here's what happened.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.430
John W. Ferryman was here to see it last month.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.240
You know, Ferryman has practically been Palm Beach in Miami,

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:49.940
but he said he wouldn't touch this.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:52.320
Now, when a man like that touched the place,

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:53.120
no one wants it.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.000
Do you know anything about architecture?

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.920
No, but I'd love to learn.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.380
So I made a drawing of the whole place, showing the hills.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:07.360
As a build-up scheme, without cutting down the hill, or having to get in the way.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.110
I made the hill fit in with the architectural scheme.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:16.700
I sent Barryman a copy last week, and his secretary wrote me a nice note, saying they were studying my plans.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:19.060
That's thrilling. Did Mr. Hammer know about it?

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.050
Not yet, but if he takes it, I'll design the buildings.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:24.590
Say, I may be an architect, yes.

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:28.620
Oh, if he only does, I'm sure it will be the most beautiful place in the world.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:29.400
It would be.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.930
If you live there, look, see what I've written.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.240
Heaven for Polly and me.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:39.730
That looks great.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:41.370
When do I move in?

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.070
Any day now.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.870
It's a lovely dream while.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:46.630
Make it come true.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:27.230
I'm a practical fool.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:58.400
I seem to do my own.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.940
I went, well, I re-

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.540
the driver went to heaven

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:13.620
Look at that.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:14.850
I am looking.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:16.220
Darn cute.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:17.830
I wonder who it could be?

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:19.030
We'll find out.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:23.180
The little red riding hood set for the wolf.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:25.160
Hello.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:26.590
Oh, hello.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:27.970
How do you do, Miss Father?

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:28.350
Hello.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:29.970
Your mother is looking for you, Pa.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.220
It was a lovely story, Mr. Adams.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.980
I'd like to hear the rest of it sometime.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:40.070
Goodbye.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:43.710
If I could hear it sometime.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:45.330
With pleasure.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:47.410
How about you, Yates?

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:48.330
No, thanks.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:50.840
You know what happens to bad little boys?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:51.760
Tell stories.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:52.980
Certainly.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:55.360
They marry the beautiful princess.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:56.790
So long.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:00.650
He'll be there.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:21.450
But he won.

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:24.820
I might win out yet.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.290
Well, miracles do happen.

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:33.280
Well, Polly, you've been out again with Mr. Adams.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:35.260
But only for a little while, Mother.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:40.040
Why a daughter of mine should fool around with a hotel clerk

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.800
when she has the opportunity of marrying one of the Boston Yeats

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.460
is more than I can understand.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:46.700
Oh, who cares about the Boston Yeats?

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.500
Anyway, Bob isn't a clerk. He's an architect.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.520
He's only clerking until he can get started.

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:56.130
One who clerks, Polly, is a clerk, and that settles it.

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.980
And I want you to remember that...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:06.660
No problem has been involved in a single scandal about Uncle Dick, Holly.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:10.840
It's a well-known fact that your uncle was drunk at the time.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:16.010
And another thing, young lady, I'm quite sure you're sitting out on the beach.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:22.360
Hey, hey, why don't you take something for that insomnia?

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.100
You ought to come out drinking so much coffee.

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:25.100
I'm sorry, sir.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:26.970
Say, any luck with the 4.30?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.370
Yes, it didn't hit me. That's the only luck I had with her.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:29.880
Mr.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.540
Mr. Hammer, I think I know what's wrong with the hotel.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.340
I think I know, too. You're fired.

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:34.820
Get your hat and my coat and get out.

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:36.700
Well, maybe the season hasn't started yet.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:38.680
Maybe the hotel hasn't opened yet.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.040
Don't worry, Mr. Hammer.

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:41.440
In a few weeks, you'll be cleaning up.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.480
Yes, and making the bed.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:43.580
Go on, get out of here.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:44.920
I can handle this rush myself.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.670
600 rooms in the hotel, and you have to sleep here.

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:48.610
How do you do, Mr. Hammer?

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:49.930
Why don't you whistle at the crossing?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.510
You're just the woman I'm looking for.

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:52.570
Now, whether you like it or not,

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.170
I'm going to tell you about Florida real estate.

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:56.590
It's the first time it's ever been mentioned down here today.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:57.990
I'm sorry, but I'm...

00:15:57.990 --> 00:15:59.870
Do you know that property values have increased?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.800
since 1929, since 1,000%?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.660
Do you know that this is the biggest development

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:04.380
since Sophie Tucker?

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.090
Do you know that Florida is the show spot of America

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.910
and Coconut Beach is the black spot of Florida?

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.530
You told me about this yesterday.

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:11.910
I know, but I left out a comma.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:14.210
Look, in a little while we're going to hold an auction sale

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:15.030
at Coconut Manor.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:16.510
It's very terrible, beautiful.

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:17.710
You must come over.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:20.030
There's going to be entertainment, sandwiches, and the auction.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.370
If you don't like auction, we can play a contract.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.050
Here it is, Coconut Manor.

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.540
42 hours from Times Square by railroad.

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:28.420
1,600 miles of the crow flies.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:29.880
1,800 of the horse flies.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:34.180
There you are, Coconut Manor, glorifying the American sewer and the Florida sucker.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.980
Why, it's the most exclusive residential district in Florida.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.040
Nobody lives there.

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:38.920
And the climate.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.580
Ask me about the climate, I dare you.

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:41.360
Very well.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:42.480
I knew that you brought it up.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:43.800
Our motto is Coconut Beach.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.540
No snow, no ice, and no business.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:47.810
Do you know that Florida is the greatest state in the Union?

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:48.410
Is it?

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:49.150
Take its climate.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:49.910
No, we took that.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:50.530
Take its fruits.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:51.670
Take the alligator pears.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.350
Take all the alligator pears and keep them.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:54.010
See if I care.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.280
Do you know how alligator pears are made?

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:57.480
Have them for slightest idea.

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:58.020
There you are.

00:16:58.100 --> 00:16:59.540
That's because you've never been an alligator.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.940
And don't let it happen again.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:04.950
Do you know that it sometimes requires years to bring the pear and the alligator together?

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:05.970
They don't like each other.

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:06.350
No.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:06.830
No.

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:11.130
Do you know how many alligator pears are sent out of this state every year and told them not to come back?

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:12.210
I don't think I do.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:13.330
All they can get a hold of.

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:16.990
Florida feeds the nation, but nobody feeds me, and that's what I want to talk to you about.

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:17.630
Mr. Hammer.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:18.230
Another thing.

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:19.250
Take our cattle raising.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:23.230
I don't mean anything personal, but here is the ideal cattle raising section.

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:25.690
We have long horns, short horns, and shoe horns.

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:28.010
Mr. Hammer, will you let me say something, please?

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.910
I hardly think so, and there's something else.

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.240
Where will you be when you're 65?

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.140
That's only about three months from now.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:38.240
If I were to buy, I should preserve some place like Palm Beach.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.070
Palm Beach?

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:41.550
The Atlantic City of yesterday, the slums of tomorrow.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:44.810
Do you know that the population of Coconut Beach has doubled in the past week?

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:45.390
Hasn't it?

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:46.550
Three Bulldogs were born.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.190
We're expecting a nanny-goes in the morning.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:50.980
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid I must be gone.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:51.780
Ah, now, don't go.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.740
Before you go, let me show you a sample of our sewer pipe we're gonna lay.

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:56.000
Look at it.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.840
Nobody can fool you on a sewer pipe, can they?

00:17:57.920 --> 00:17:58.580
A woman like you.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:17:59.980
Now, this is the eight-inch...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.160
But, of course, all property owners will be allowed to roll in the sides of the pipe.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:05.320
In case of a tie, it goes to the Supreme Court.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:08.240
And I can give you a little inside information in advance.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.280
The Chief Justice is crazy about this pipe stower.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.100
Here, put it in your pocket. I'll see you later.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.710
Mr. Hammer, I can't use this. I don't...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:39.980
Yes, I fought on 318. Is that so? Where'd you get it? Oh, you want some? Oh, that's different. Have you got any ice?

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:46.240
No, I haven't. This is Copernet Beach. No snow and no ice. Get some onions. That'll make your eyes water.

